    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0628" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg548"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Lord
                            Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2343.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In further reply to your note of the
                    2d instant, I have now the honor to inform you that the Secretary of the
                    Treasury wrote, on the 21st idem, that all the United States customs officers on
                    the northern frontier had been instructed not hereafter to display official
                    flags if their offices are located on British North American territory.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
